   {text:'A diagonal matrix containing only individual asset variances — all off-diagonal covariances set to zero.',correct:true,
    why:'lam=1.0: Sigma = (0)*Sigma_emp + (1)*diag. np.diag(np.diag(M)) extracts M\'s diagonal into a new diagonal-only matrix. Full cross-asset correlations are discarded.'},
   {text:'The identity matrix, normalizing all variances to 1.0 and zeroing correlations.',correct:false,
    why:'Wrong — diag = np.diag(np.diag(Sigma_emp)) preserves the original variances from Sigma_emp; it doesn\'t normalize them to 1.'},
   {text:'A zero matrix, effectively giving equal weights to all assets by making the inverse undefined.',correct:false,
