<strong>r_s = α + β·r_m + ε</strong>:
<ul style="margin:.5rem 0 .5rem 1.2rem;line-height:1.8">
  <li><strong>α</strong> (alpha): the strategy's market-independent return — what's left after explaining away β units of market. The "skill" part that can't be cheaply replicated.</li>
